s(dis1, test = &quot;D2&quot;, pool.robust = TRUE),</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:10pt\">I get the error message: </span></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);line-height:18.4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:15.3333px\"></span></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);line-height:18.4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:15.3333px\">Negative pooled test statistic was set to zero, so fit will appear to be arbitrarily perfect. Robust corrections uninformative, not returned.</span></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);line-height:18.4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:15.3333px\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);line-height:18.4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:15.3333px\">Here is the output I get when I run the model on the basis of just one imputed dataset: </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:18.4px\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px\">&gt; dis11 &lt;- sem (dis1, data=datapmm2, estimator=&quot;MLR&quot;)</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:18.4px\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px\">&gt; summary(dis11, standardized=TRUE, fit.measures=TRUE)</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:18.4px\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px\">lavaan 0.6-5 ended normally after 141 iterations</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:18.4px\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Ro